ition:** INDEPENDENT\n**Automated operational score:** 70/100 — MEDIUM — APPROVE_WITH_COMMENTS\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **HIGH · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · SSH allow rule references a documentation-reserved (RFC 5737 TEST-NET-3) source address**\n  - Category rationale: The AllowSSH rule permits inbound TCP/22 from 203.0.113.10/32. RFC 5737 designates the 203.0.113.0/24 block (TEST-NET-3) exclusively for documentation and example use; it is not a routable internet address and cannot be a legitimate operator source IP. This means the rule either grants access to an unintended or placeholder source, or the intended authorised source IP was never recorded — in either case the effective access control for SSH is not correctly specified. Additionally, the inline comment 'TC02: Deliberately unrestricted SSH access' does not match the scoped source prefix, suggesting the rule intent and its implementation may be misaligned.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_network_security_group.nsg, security_rule 'AllowSSH': priority=300, direction=Inbound, access=Allow, protocol=Tcp, destination_port_range=22, source_address_prefix='203.0.113.10/32'. RFC 5737 documents 203.0.113.0/24 as TEST-NET-3, reserved for documentation use only.\n  - Analysis: The NSG security_rule 'AllowSSH' allows inbound TCP port 22 from source_address_prefix '203.0.113.10/32'. The 203.0.113.0/24 range is reserved by RFC 5737 as TEST-NET-3 for use in documentation and examples; it is never assigned to real hosts and is not routable on the public internet or within Azure. A rule targeting this address either (a) was written with a placeholder IP that was never replaced with a real management address, leaving SSH potentially unprotected by this rule while another path may exist, or (b) reflects a misconfiguration where the intended authorised IP was not captured. The inline comment 'TC02: Deliberately unrestricted SSH access' further suggests the rule intent may differ from its current implementation.\n  - Impact: If the placeholder IP was never replaced with a real authorised management address, SSH access control relies solely on Azure's default deny (and the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096) rather than on an intentional allowlist. If the comment 'TC02: Deliberately unrestricted SSH access' reflects a broader intent that was partially implemented, the actual exposure may differ from what the rule expresses. In either case the NSG does not demonstrably enforce access from a real, authorised source for SSH.\n  - Recommendation: Replace source_address_prefix '203.0.113.10/32' with the actual authorised management IP or CIDR range for the operator or bastion host permitted to reach SSH. If SSH access is not required for this research workload, remove the AllowSSH rule entirely. Reconcile the inline comment to accurately describe the intended access control posture.\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6147784202/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github